    <dashboard name='Story 1' type='storyboard'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>LONDON SPORT : DIAGNOSE THEN PRIORITISE</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <style>
        <style-rule element='table'>
          <format attr='background-color' value='#f7f1f6' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='story-description'>
          <format attr='border-style' value='dashed' />
          <format attr='font-size' value='12' />
          <format attr='background-color' value='#fffef5af' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='story-point-caption'>
          <format attr='width' value='197' />
          <format attr='font-size' value='14' />
        </style-rule>
        <style-rule element='story-title'>
          <format attr='font-size' value='20' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size sizing-mode='automatic' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98120' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99034' x='483' y='940'>
            <zone h='4935' id='3' type-v2='title' w='99034' x='483' y='940' />
            <zone fixed-size='134' h='15746' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='99034' x='483' y='5875' />
            <zone h='77439' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='99034' x='483' y='21621'>
              <flipboard active-id='6' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='The Landscape' captured-sheet='Classification Toggle Map' id='1' />
                  <story-point caption='The Equity Problem' captured-sheet='Equity Scatter' id='2'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Equity Scatter'>
                        <style delta-type='added'>
                          <style-rule element='axis'>
                            <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.1x8xs9f03uydwx15yhoh01od4sgt].[avg:equity_gap:qk]' field-type='quantitative' max='20.630762174766868' min='0.0' range-type='fixed' scope='rows' type='space' />
                            <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.1x8xs9f03uydwx15yhoh01od4sgt].[avg:demand_score:qk]' field-type='quantitative' max='84.35546875' min='0.0' range-type='fixed' scope='cols' type='space' />
                          </style-rule>
                        </style>
                        <selection-collection />
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='Classification Confidence' captured-sheet='Classification Instability' id='3'>
                    <capturedDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Classification Instability'>
                        <selection-collection />
                      </worksheet>
                    </capturedDeltas>
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='Supporting Evidence' captured-sheet='Dash for story' id='4' />
                  <story-point caption='Ethnicity Equity Gaps' captured-sheet='Ethinicity equity' id='5'>
                    <currentDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Ethinicity equity'>
                        <selection-collection />
                      </worksheet>
                    </currentDeltas>
                    <capturedDeltas />
                  </story-point>
                  <story-point caption='Where To Act' captured-sheet='Interventions' id='6'>
                    <currentDeltas>
                      <worksheet name='Interventions'>
                        <selection-collection />
                      </worksheet>
                    </currentDeltas>
                    <capturedDeltas />
                  </story-point>
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='20682' hidden='true' id='6' story-point-id='1' type-v2='text' w='24683' x='63669' y='74853'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>London&apos;s 32 boroughs, each classified into one of nine categories based on how local activity supply matches local demand. The map lets you toggle between three different threshold methods to see how sensitive each borough&apos;s label is to that choice</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='25264' hidden='true' id='7' story-point-id='2' type-v2='text' w='27399' x='5914' y='49706'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Kingston upon Thames, Richmond, and Wandsworth are all classified as well-served or adequately served overall  yet they carry London&apos;s largest equity gaps. Their poorest residents are significantly more inactive than the borough average suggests, a pattern a simple supply-demand label alone would miss</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='26204' hidden='true' id='8' story-point-id='3' type-v2='text' w='26735' x='61135' y='61222'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Not every borough&apos;s classification is equally certain. Twelve of the 32 boroughs sit close enough to a threshold boundary that their label changes depending on whether tertile, median, or quartile splits are used. Rather than hide this, each borough is flagged with its stability status alongside its classification</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='27027' hidden='true' id='9' story-point-id='4' type-v2='text' w='26192' x='61376' y='59812'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Some boroughs show very low recorded activity but that isn&apos;t always a real gap in provision. Enfield and Redbridge, for example, have confirmed leisure centres that simply don&apos;t appear correctly in the underlying provider data, a distinction the dashboard makes explicit</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='30670' hidden='true' id='10' story-point-id='5' type-v2='text' w='21967' x='77670' y='57697'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Deprivation isn&apos;t the only axis of inequality. Looking at ethnicity instead, the largest activity gaps appear in Haringey, Southwark, and Lambeth&apos;s Black communities — boroughs that don&apos;t show up at all in the deprivation-based equity analysis. Equity, it turns out, is multi-dimensional</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='28437' id='11' story-point-id='6' type-v2='text' w='20278' x='78274' y='61810'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Seven boroughs are classified as genuine deserts, blind spots, or at risk of becoming one. Each is paired with its dominant barrier ,whether people can&apos;t find activities (an opportunity gap) or don&apos;t feel able to take part (an ability gap) , which turns the classification into a concrete next step</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{3B3C9A2C-3E89-474E-AB97-CA04A3295551}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
